{"qid":"Q760","names":["Saint Lucia"],"title":"Saint Lucia","endonym":{"native":"Saint Lucia","lang":"en"},"capsule":"Saint Lucia achieved independence from Britain on 22 February 1979 as a constitutional monarchy within the Commonwealth, following a period as an associated state with full internal self-government from 1967. The island's economy is anchored in banana exports and tourism; its political life has alternated between the Saint Lucia Labour Party and the United Workers Party since independence. Saint Lucia retains the British monarch as head of state, represented by a governor-general, and maintains membership in CARICOM and the Organisation of Eastern Caribbean States.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Saint Lucia's territory—the island of 617 km² in the Eastern Caribbean—is precisely defined; there are no territorial disputes.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Saint Lucia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Lucia"},{"label":"Britannica: Saint Lucia","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Saint-Lucia"}],"britannica":"place/Saint-Lucia","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Saint Lucia","rulers":[{"qid":"Q716020","name":"John Compton","start":1979,"end":1979,"image":"John Compton.png","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/John%20Compton.png?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY 3.0","artist":"Saint Lucian goverment","attributionRequired":true}},{"qid":"Q966659","name":"Allan Louisy","start":1979,"end":1981,"image":null},{"qid":"Q9682","name":"Elizabeth II","start":1979,"end":2022,"image":"Queen Elizabeth II official portrait for 1959 tour (retouched)